{
  "name": "duplicate-vulns",
  "integration": "maze-security",
  "description": "REGRESSION LOCK. An investigation fanned out over its related_scanner_findings used to contribute one COPY OF ITSELF per finding. group_investigations calls add_to_asset_map once per related finding and that function appended build_vulnerability(inv) unconditionally, so two findings resolving to one asset -- either both carrying the same asset_name, or both nameless and falling back to the same scanner_finding_hash asset segment -- put the same Vulnerability on the asset twice, under the same id (investigation.id). N findings naming one asset produced N copies of one finding. add_to_asset_map now keys on (asset, investigation.id) and counts an investigation once per asset, while every finding still merges its metadata.\n\nAll 99 investigations here name ONE asset and each carries two findings that reach it: 1-50 name it explicitly through asset_name, 51-99 leave asset_name absent or empty so both findings fall back to the hash's asset segment. Both duplication paths are therefore live.\n\nThe count is pinned with the 99-child cap rather than an equality assertion, because the harness can only assert a MINIMUM vulnerability count: 99 investigations must yield exactly 99 findings, and duplicating each one makes it 198, which the child_caps invariant rejects. maze_finding_count is asserted alongside it because the script computes that attribute from the same list before the cap applies, so it pins the count exactly even if the runtime were to collapse same-id vulnerabilities on the way out.\n\nThe metadata assertions are the other half of the fix. inv-dup-001 splits its metadata across its two findings -- the first carries asset_type and scanner, the second cloud_platform, region, account_id and asset_id -- so an implementation that deduped by keeping only the first finding per asset and dropping the rest would lose four attributes and fail here.\n\nnamespaced_ids is skipped for the reason recorded in identity-convergence: Maze ids are bare scanner-supplied names with no tenant scope, and under no-id-match they do not drive matching.",
  "kwargs": {
    "url": "$BASE",
    "api_key": "fixture-key",
    "days_back": "7"
  },
